2026-10-30 04:42:10 INFO areno.api.trainers.policy_only.PolicyOnlyTrainer policy_only.py:723 - rollout_completion={"kind": "rollout", "epoch": 0, "step": 12, "prompt_idx": 0, "sample_idx": 0, "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Nico borrows 3 books from the library on Monday.  On Monday, he reads the first book with a total of 20 pages.  On Tuesday, he reads the second book with a total of 12 pages.  On Wednesday, he reads the third book.  If he has read a total of 51 pages from Monday to Wednesday, how many pages did he read on Wednesday?\nSolution:", "decoded_prompt": "<|im_start|>user\nSolve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Nico borrows 3 books from the library on Monday.  On Monday, he reads the first book with a total of 20 pages.  On Tuesday, he reads the second book with a total of 12 pages.  On Wednesday, he reads the third book.  If he has read a total of 51 pages from Monday to Wednesday, how many pages did he read on Wednesday?\nSolution:<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n", "completion": "<think>\nOkay, let me try to work through this problem step by step. So, Nico borrows 3 books on Monday. Then he reads each book with different page counts: 20 pages on Monday, 12 pages on Tuesday, and then some amount on Wednesday. The total pages read from Monday to Wednesday is given as 51. We need to find out how many pages he read on Wednesday.\n\nFirst, let me write down the information:\n\n- Monday: 20 pages\n- Tuesday: 12 pages\n- Wednesday: ?\n- Total pages from Monday to Wednesday: 51\n\nSo, if I add up the pages from Monday and Tuesday, that will give me the total pages read on those two days. Then I can subtract that sum from 51 to find out how many pages he read on Wednesday.\n\nLet me check that. Total pages = sum of pages on Monday + pages on Tuesday + pages on Wednesday.\n\nSo, substituting:\n\nTotal pages = 20 (Monday) + 12 (Tuesday) + pages Wednesday = 51.\n\nSo, solving for pages Wednesday:\n\npages Wednesday = total - (pages Monday + pages Tuesday) = 51 - (20 + 12).\n\nCalculating that, 20 + 12 is 32, so 51 minus 32 equals 19. Therefore, Nico read 19 pages on Wednesday.\n\nWait, let me verify again. Let me add 20 and 12 first. 20 plus 12 is indeed 32. Then 51 minus 32 is 19. Yep, that seems right. So, the answer is 19 pages.\n\nHmm, that seems straightforward. Maybe I made a mistake in the problem? Let me check once more.\n\nWait, the problem says \"he has read a total of 51 pages from Monday to Wednesday.\" So adding Monday (20) + Tuesday (12) + Wednesday (unknown) equals 51. Yep, that's correct. 20 + 12 is 32, so Wednesday is 51 minus 32, which is 19. Okay, I think that's accurate.\n\nIs there any possibility that I misread the problem? Let me check again. The problem says he borrows 3 books on Monday. Then reads the first book with 20 pages on Monday, the second with 12 on Tuesday. Then on Wednesday reads the third. So, three books, two days. Total pages 51. Therefore, pages on Wednesday is 51 minus first two days. Which is 19. Yes, that makes sense.\n\nI think I'm confident with this answer. 19 pages on Wednesday.\n</think>\n\nNico borrowed 3 books from the library on Monday. On Monday, he read 20 pages, and on Tuesday, he read 12 pages. The total pages he read from Monday to Wednesday is given as 51. To find the number of pages he read on Wednesday, we add the pages from the first two days and subtract that from the total:\n\n$$\n\\text{Pages on Wednesday} = 51 - (20 + 12) = 51 - 32 = 19\n$$\n\n### Final Answer:\n$$\n\\boxed{19}\n$$<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "Nico borrows 3 books from the library on Monday.  On Monday, he reads the first book with a total of 20 pages.  On Tuesday, he reads the second book with a total of 12 pages.  On Wednesday, he reads the third book.  If he has read a total of 51 pages from Monday to Wednesday, how many pages did he read on Wednesday?", "answer": "From Monday to Tuesday, Nico reads a total of 20 + 12 = <<20+12=32>>32 pages.\nOn Wednesday, he read a total of 51 - 32 = <<51-32=19>>19 pages.\n#### 19", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Nico borrows 3 books from the library on Monday.  On Monday, he reads the first book with a total of 20 pages.  On Tuesday, he reads the second book with a total of 12 pages.  On Wednesday, he reads the third book.  If he has read a total of 51 pages from Monday to Wednesday, how many pages did he read on Wednesday?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["19"], "solution": "19"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 74035, 31632, 1811, 220, 18, 6467, 504, 279, 6733, 389, 7014, 13, 220, 1913, 7014, 11, 566, 15804, 279, 1156, 2311, 448, 264, 2790, 315, 220, 17, 15, 6816, 13, 220, 1913, 7589, 11, 566, 15804, 279], "response_tokens": [151667, 198, 32313, 11, 1077, 752, 1430, 311, 975, 1526, 419, 3491, 3019, 553, 3019, 13, 2055, 11, 74035, 31632, 1811, 220, 18, 6467, 389, 7014, 13, 5005, 566, 15804, 1817, 2311, 448, 2155, 2150, 14579, 25, 220, 17, 15, 6816, 389, 7014, 11, 220, 16, 17, 6816, 389, 7589, 11, 323, 1221, 1045, 3311, 389, 7920, 13, 576, 2790, 6816, 1349, 504, 7014]}
