2026-10-30 04:52:48 INFO areno.api.trainers.policy_only.PolicyOnlyTrainer policy_only.py:723 - rollout_completion={"kind": "rollout", "epoch": 0, "step": 20, "prompt_idx": 0, "sample_idx": 0, "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Michelangelo has 28 ceilings to paint. This week, he paints 12 of them. Next week, he will paint 1/4 the number of ceilings he did this week. How many ceilings will be left to paint after next week?\nSolution:", "decoded_prompt": "<|im_start|>user\nSolve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Michelangelo has 28 ceilings to paint. This week, he paints 12 of them. Next week, he will paint 1/4 the number of ceilings he did this week. How many ceilings will be left to paint after next week?\nSolution:<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n", "completion": "<think>\nOkay, let's see. Michelangelo has 28 ceilings to paint. This week, he paints 12 of them. Then next week, he paints 1/4 the number he did this week. I need to find out how many ceilings are left to paint after next week. Hmm, let me break this down step by step.\n\nFirst, let me figure out how many ceilings are left after this week. If there are 28 ceilings total and he paints 12, then the remaining ones would be 28 minus 12. Let me compute that. 28 minus 12 is 16. So, after the first week, there are 16 ceilings left. But then next week, he paints 1/4 of the number he did this week. This week he painted 12, so 1/4 of 12? Hmm, 12 divided by 4 is 3. So next week, he paints 3 ceilings. Wait, so subtracting that from the remaining ones?\n\nSo the remaining numbers after the first week are 16. Then, subtract 3, right? 16 minus 3 equals 13. Therefore, after next week, there should be 13 ceilings left to paint. Let me check again to be sure. \n\nTotal ceilings: 28. Painted this week: 12. So left: 28 - 12 = 16. Then next week, he paints 1/4 of 12, which is 3. So 16 - 3 = 13. Yeah, that seems right. \n\nWait, but let me make sure I didn't mix up the fractions. 1/4 of 12 is 3, yes. So subtracting 3 from the 16 leaves 13. So the answer should be 13. \n\nAlternatively, maybe I can approach it in another way. Let's think about the total. The total ceilings is 28. He paints 12 at this week. So 28 - 12 = 16. Then next week, painting 1/4. Since 1/4 is 3, then 16 - 3 = 13. Same result. \n\nI think that's correct. No mistakes here. So the final answer is 13 ceilings left to paint.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe number of ceilings left to paint after next week is \\boxed{13}.\n</think>\n\nTo determine how many ceilings Michelangelo will leave to paint after next week, we follow these steps:\n\n1. **Initial total ceilings to paint:** 28 ceilings  \n2. **Ceilings painted this week:** 12  \n3. **Ceilings left after this week:**  \n   $$\n   28 - 12 = 16 \\text{ ceilings left}\n   $$\n\n4. **Ceilings painted next week:** This means he paints $ \\frac{1}{4} $ of 12.  \n   $$\n   \\frac{1}{4} \\times 12 = 3 \\text{ ceilings}\n   $$\n\n5. **Ceilings left after next week:**  \n   $$\n   16 - 3 = 13\n   $$\n\nThus, after next week, Michelangelo will have $\\boxed{13}$ ceilings left to paint.<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "Michelangelo has 28 ceilings to paint. This week, he paints 12 of them. Next week, he will paint 1/4 the number of ceilings he did this week. How many ceilings will be left to paint after next week?", "answer": "After this week, Michelangelo will have 28-12=<<28-12=16>>16 more ceilings to paint.\nNext week, Michelangelo will paint 12/4=<<12/4=3>>3 ceilings.\nMichelangelo will have 16-3=<<16-3=13>>13 more ceilings to paint.\n#### 13", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Michelangelo has 28 ceilings to paint. This week, he paints 12 of them. Next week, he will paint 1/4 the number of ceilings he did this week. How many ceilings will be left to paint after next week?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["13"], "solution": "13"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 44406, 87910, 702, 220, 17, 23, 55714, 311, 6177, 13, 1096, 2003, 11, 566, 56848, 220, 16, 17, 315, 1105, 13, 9295, 2003, 11, 566, 686, 6177, 220, 16, 14, 19, 279, 1372, 315, 55714, 566, 1521], "response_tokens": [151667, 198, 32313, 11, 1077, 594, 1490, 13, 44406, 87910, 702, 220, 17, 23, 55714, 311, 6177, 13, 1096, 2003, 11, 566, 56848, 220, 16, 17, 315, 1105, 13, 5005, 1790, 2003, 11, 566, 56848, 220, 16, 14, 19, 279, 1372, 566, 1521, 419, 2003, 13, 358, 1184, 311, 1477, 700, 1246, 1657, 55714, 525, 2115, 311, 6177, 1283, 1790, 2003, 13, 88190, 11]}
