g with 15. She eats 4, so 15 - 4 = 11. Then she eats another 2, so 11 - 2 = 9. Then she takes 2, so 9 - 2 = 7. Then eats 5, so 7 - 5 = 2. Yeah, same answer. So, 2 slices left. Hmm, but maybe I need to do this more carefully.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I should add up all the slices she ate and subtract from 15. Let's see:\n\nBreakfast: 4\n\nLunch: 2\n\nSnack: 2\n\nDinner: 5\n\nTotal eaten: 4 + 2 + 2 + 5 = 13 slices. So, initial 15 minus 13 is 2 slices left. Yep, same result.\n\nWait, just to be thorough, let me make sure I didn't make any mistakes in the addition. 4 plus 2 is 6, plus 2 more is 8, plus 5 is 13. Yep. 15-13 is 2. So, the answer should be 2.\n\nBut let me think again to make sure there isn't anything else I'm missing. The problem says she takes two slices as a snack after eating 4 and 2. So, those are separate from the breakfast, lunch, and dinner. So, adding 2 slices as snack is an additional snack, so those 2 slices are subtracted. So, yes, 15 - 4 -2 -2 -5 = 2. That's 15 - 4 =11, minus 2 is 9, minus 2 is 7, minus 5 is 2.\n\nAlternatively, maybe write it out step by step:\n\nStart: 15 slices.\n\nBreakfast: 15 - 4 = 11.\n\nLunch: 11 - 2 = 9.\n\nSnack: 9 - 2 = 7.\n\nDinner: 7 - 5 = 2.\n\nYep, same result. So, I think that's correct.\n\nWait, but let me check if the snack count is included in the 4, 2, 2, 5. So, the problem says \"takes two slices as a snack. Finally, she consumes 5 slices for dinner.\" So, the snack is separate when eating. So, yes, those 2 are subtracted. Therefore, the answer is 2.\n\nI don't see any mistakes here. The answer is 2 slices left.\n</think>\n\nTo determine how many slices of pizza are left, we start with the initial number of slices in the fridge and subtract the total slices consumed during breakfast, lunch, snack, and dinner.\n\n1. Initial number of slices: $15$\n2. Breakfast: $15 - 4 = 11$\n3. Lunch: $11 - 2 = 9$\n4. Snack: $9 - 2 = 7$\n5. Dinner: $7 - 5 = 2$\n\nThus, the final number of slices left is:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{2}\n$$<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "Blanch has 15 slices of pizza in the fridge. During breakfast, she eats 4 slices. At lunch, Blanch eats 2 slices, then takes two slices as a snack. Finally, she consumes 5 slices for dinner. How many slices of pizza are left?", "answer": "During breakfast, Blanch has 15 - 4 = <<15-4=11>>11 slices left.\nAt lunch, she still has 11 - 2 = <<11-2=9>>9 slices left.\nAfter the snack, there are still 9 - 2 = <<9-2=7>>7 slices left.\nFinally after dinner, Blanch has 7 - 5 = <<7-5=2>>2 slices left.\n#### 2", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Blanch has 15 slices of pizza in the fridge. During breakfast, she eats 4 slices. At lunch, Blanch eats 2 slices, then takes two slices as a snack. Finally, she consumes 5 slices for dinner. How many slices of pizza are left?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["2"], "solution": "2"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 91429, 702, 220, 16, 20, 34254, 315, 22502, 304, 279, 37581, 13, 11954, 17496, 11, 1340, 49677, 220, 19, 34254, 13, 2411, 15786, 11, 91429, 49677, 220, 17, 34254, 11, 1221, 4990, 1378, 34254, 438, 264, 39359], "response_tokens": [151667, 198, 32313, 11, 1077, 752, 1430, 311, 7071, 700, 419, 22502, 3491, 13, 2055, 11, 91429, 8471, 448, 220, 16, 20, 34254, 304, 279, 37581, 13, 5005, 1340, 49677, 1045, 518, 17496, 11, 1045, 2337, 15786, 11, 4990, 1378, 438, 264, 39359, 11, 323, 49677, 220, 20, 369, 13856, 13, 358, 1184, 311, 1477, 700, 1246, 1657, 34254, 525, 2115, 13, 6771, 752]}
