n. So, the answer should be $97.\n</think>\n\nAmy starts with $100, and each doll costs $1. She purchases 3 dolls, which costs $3. The amount of money she has left is calculated as:\n\n$$\n100 - 3 = 97\n$$\n\nThus, Amy has $\\boxed{97}$ dollars left.<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "Amy's grandfather gave her $100 for her birthday. Amy bought 3 dolls, each of which cost $1. How much money does Amy have left?", "answer": "The cost of the dolls is 3 × $1 = $<<3*1=3>>3.\nAmy has $100 − $3 = $97 left.\n#### 97", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Amy's grandfather gave her $100 for her birthday. Amy bought 3 dolls, each of which cost $1. How much money does Amy have left?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["97"], "solution": "97"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 28693, 594, 37850, 6551, 1059, 400, 16, 15, 15, 369, 1059, 15198, 13, 28693, 10788, 220, 18, 63781, 11, 1817, 315, 892, 2783, 400, 16, 13, 2585, 1753, 3220, 1558, 28693, 614, 2115, 5267, 36842, 25, 151645], "response_tokens": [151667, 198, 32313, 11, 1077, 594, 1490, 13, 28693, 594, 37850, 6551, 1059, 400, 16, 15, 15, 11, 323, 1340, 10788, 220, 18, 63781, 13, 8886, 7649, 7049, 400, 16, 13, 358, 1184, 311, 1477, 700, 1246, 1753, 3220, 1340, 702, 2115, 13, 88190, 13, 97593, 11, 1077, 594, 1438, 419, 1495, 3019, 553, 3019, 13, 4710, 5338, 11, 1340, 8471, 448, 400, 16]}
