rnatively, maybe I need to interpret the problem differently. Let me re-read it: \"A snake's head is one-tenth its length. If a snake is 10 feet long, calculate the length of the rest of its body minus the head.\" So, total length is 10 feet. Head is 1/10 of total. Then rest of body is total length minus head. Then rest of body minus head is (total length - head) - head. So that would be total length - 2*head. \n\nAlternatively, since the head is 1/10, rest of body is 1 - 1/10 = 9/10 of the total length. Then subtract the head. Which would be 9/10 total - 1/10 total = 8/10 total, which is 8/10 of 10 feet, which is 8 feet. So yes, that seems correct. \n\nWait, so maybe another way: The rest of the body is the total minus 1 foot. Then subtracting the head, which is 1 foot, so 9 -1 = 8. \n\nAlternatively, maybe the problem is expecting a different interpretation. But no, the way it's phrased, \"the length of the rest of its body minus the head\", so it's body length minus head, so (10 -1) -1 = 8. \n\nTherefore, the answer should be 8 feet. Let me check once more. Total length 10 feet. Head is 1 foot. So rest of body is 10 - 1 = 9. Then rest of body minus head is 9 - 1 = 8. Yep, that's straightforward. \n\nI think that's it. There's no tricks here. The key is to figure out the head's length, subtract it from the total length, and then subtract the head again to get the rest minus head. So answer is 8.\n</think>\n\nTo solve the problem, we start by understanding the given information:\n\n- A snake's head is **one-tenth** of its total length.\n- The snake is **10 feet long**.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Calculate the length of the head\nSince the head is one-tenth of the length of the snake:\n$$\n\\text{Head length} = \\frac{1}{10} \\times 10 = 1 \\text{ foot}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Calculate the length of the rest of the body\nThe rest of the body is the total length of the snake minus the head:\n$$\n\\text{Rest of the body} = 10 - 1 = 9 \\text{ feet}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Find the length of the rest of the body minus the head\nThe problem asks for the length of the rest of the body minus the head, which can be calculated as:\n$$\n\\text{Answer} = 9 - 1 = 8 \\text{ feet}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Final Answer:\n$$\n\\boxed{8}\n$$<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "A snake's head is one-tenth its length. If a snake is 10 feet long, calculate the length of the rest of its body minus the head.", "answer": "A snake's head is one-tenth its length, which is 1/10*10 = <<1/10*10=1>>1 foot.\nSince the snake's head is 1 foot, the rest of its body is 10-1 = <<10-1=9>>9 feet long.\n#### 9", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: A snake's head is one-tenth its length. If a snake is 10 feet long, calculate the length of the rest of its body minus the head.\nSolution:", "solutions": ["9"], "solution": "9"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 362, 25265, 594, 1968, 374, 825, 2385, 20684, 1181, 3084, 13, 1416, 264, 25265, 374, 220, 16, 15, 7541, 1293, 11, 11047, 279, 3084, 315, 279, 2732, 315, 1181, 2487, 27283, 279, 1968, 624, 36842, 25, 151645], "response_tokens": [151667, 198, 32313, 11, 773, 358, 1184, 311, 7071, 700, 279, 3084, 315, 279, 2732, 315, 279, 25265, 594, 2487, 27283, 279, 1968, 13, 6771, 752, 1191, 553, 8660, 279, 3491, 13, 576, 25265, 594, 1968, 374, 825, 2385, 20684, 315, 1181, 2790, 3084, 13, 1416, 279, 4361, 25265, 374, 220, 16, 15, 7541, 1293, 11, 1221, 279, 1968, 374, 220, 16, 14, 16]}
